# Spec Template

Copy this template for durable product, feature, system, or repository-behavior specs. Use it when a change needs stable requirements, source paths, acceptance criteria, and validation evidence without introducing new harness config fields.

````markdown
# {Feature Or System} Spec

## Goal

{State the user-facing or repository-facing outcome and why it matters.}

## Profile

| Field | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Harness config | `docs/harness-engineering/harness-engineering.json` |
| Status | draft, active, or deprecated |
| Domain | {business, platform, docs, validation, architecture} |
| Primary owner | {team, agent, or role} |
| Review cadence | {per change, weekly, release} |

## Sources Of Truth

| Surface | Path | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Context map | `CLAUDE.md` | First-step instructions |
| Architecture | `ARCHITECTURE.md` | Structural constraints |
| Implementation | `{source path}` | Behavior governed by this spec |
| Validation | `{command or script}` | Evidence this spec is satisfied |

## Requirements

1. {Requirement with observable behavior.}
2. {Requirement with acceptance criteria.}
3. {Requirement with validation surface.}

## Non-Goals

- {Adjacent feature or integration intentionally outside this spec.}
- {Operational surface owned by another workflow or integration pack.}

## Acceptance Criteria

| Criterion | Evidence |
| --- | --- |
| {criterion} | `{path or command}` |
| {criterion} | `{path or command}` |

## Validation

```bash
{command}
```

## Update Rule

When implementation, docs, or validation changes affect this spec, update this file and the proof packet in the same change set.
````
